[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_u4wlr")
dialogue_id = "debate_environmental_monitoring"
record_title = "Debate Speech: Observing Nature"
text = "PAGE: scribe(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
scribe: The Historian often dismisses our ancient rites as idle contemplation, demanding physical proof from the divine.
scribe: Such views are blinded by a lack of patience.
scribe: The Enlightened One's wisdom is a seed, planted in the minds of the faithful to sprout in the fullness of time.
scribe: At the dawn of this era, a shrine was consecrated on an island in a lake.
scribe: The priests there were inspired into a ritual of patience: to meditate daily upon the exact line where the gate's pillars meet the water.
scribe: To an impatient mind, such practice appears an exercise in futility.
scribe: But consider the fruits of this unwavering devotion!
scribe: Through their steadfast vigilance, the priests began to record the swelling of the tides.
scribe: They learned to measure the heat of the air and foresee the coming tempests.
scribe: Their faith was a lens through which the world revealed its secrets.
scribe: Divine wisdom is profound and subtle.
scribe: It does not merely hand us unearned revelations.
scribe: It commands us to cultivate the patience required to comprehend the universe.
scribe: True stewardship of our environment cannot be achieved through the arbitrary whims of ten thousand shards.
scribe: It requires a shared vision, uniting us in the sacred journey to everlasting prosperity."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
